---
title: Sea Salt Ice Cream
author: Babish
servings: 6
cuisine: Dessert
diet: GlutenFree
source: https://www.babi.sh/recipes/seasalticecream
image: https://i.pinimg.com/originals/5f/d2/bb/5fd2bb08f5f1fd1819ab6586013e8458.jpg
---

Mix @milk{1.5%cup} and @heavy cream{1.5%cup} in a #saucepan.

In a #small bowl{}, whisk @egg yolks{4} with @sugar{3/4%cup} until thin, pale, and ribbon-y.

Heat milk-cream mixture on medium-low heat until barely simmering.

Still whisking the egg mixture, slowly incorporate about 1 cup of the milk-cream mixture.

When mixture is smooth, pour it back into the milk-cream mixture

Continue to heat over medium-low heat until it reaches about 170°F, or is nice and thick.  It will lightly coat the back of a spoon. Stir constantly. Be sure to not let the mixture boil at any point, or it will curdle.

Strain through cheesecloth.

Add @vanilla extract{1%tbsp}. Slowly add the @sea salt{1%tsp}(heaping) and stir. Continue to add sea salt until satisfied with the taste.

> If you want blue color, 2 drops green dye 8 drops blue dye.

Mix for about 25 minutes per instructions of your Ice cream mixer.

Let rest in freezer for at least 6 hours.